WEBVTT

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:33.990
Here I thought we'd do a little seascape that's right off of the California, Oregon coast.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:37.480
And I've taken the liberty, because we do have time restraints here,

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:41.790
of going ahead and covering a black canvas with transparent color.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:46.620
Now, what I've done, in the center here, I've put alizarin crimson,

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.140
right in the center and going out in both directions.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:55.850
And around that, valo blue. And on the bottom, same thing.

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:59.380
So we have a circle here of crimson protruding in both directions.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.250
and blue around the edges, okay?

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.180
Now, let's take the one-inch brush

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:08.200
and a little bit of titanium white paint,

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:11.500
and let's figure out here where we want the sun to be.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:13.960
And we're gonna start, say, right about here,

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:17.060
and we'll make little tiny X's or criss-cross strokes.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:19.710
Just begin working them out,

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.290
never going back toward the center,

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:23.390
always working outward,

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:25.870
because you're gonna soon be picking up the blue color.

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:29.630
Let that run right on out like so.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:35.600
There we go. See now how it's picking up the blue?

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:45.180
Let me clean the brush. We can brighten it up just a little bit more.

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:50.480
A little more titanium white.

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:52.450
Be sure your brush is clean and dry.

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:55.540
Right into the center, working outward.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:03.700
There we go.

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:05.680
Look at that son of a gun shine now.

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:10.050
Work it all the way out to the outside edges here.

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:14.840
Okay.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.600
Now with a large brush, we're gonna go in and blend this.

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:20.940
Still making the criss-cross strokes.

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:23.590
There we go.

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:24.310
Gentle.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:29.320
Just let it go back and forth just to blend the colors together.

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:37.200
There. Very carefully take the brush marks out.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:43.110
Okay, let's wash this old big brush out.

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:48.300
There we go.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.680
Now, if you wanted to make it a little bit brighter,

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:56.320
we can add just the slightest amount of cad yellow and white.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:02:59.960
Now, you have to be very careful with this because if the...

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.040
When the yellow touches the blue, we've got a green sky.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.460
So all we want to do is right around in here,

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:08.180
put a little bit of yellow, just a tiny bit.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:13.930
That's enough because we're getting very close to the blue.

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:17.850
Now once again with a large brush, we'll blend this out.

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:27.170
Take out the brush strokes, and we've got the beginnings

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:29.150
of a beautiful little sunset here.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:34.510
Let's use the fan brush and we'll take some Van Dyke Brown

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:38.480
